architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:7:The application is nominally layered as Vue entry/app shell → UI components/composables/stores/tools → command/operation sequences → domain world/process-tree/calculation model → rendering/persistence/integration services. In practice, several boundaries are porous: the domain root imports command and service layers, the canvas component directly constructs tools and operations, persistence reconstructs every operation class with a large switch, and multiple stores/components duplicate or bypass the canonical `World` ownership model. The largest god-modules are `SvgCanvas.vue`, `ProjectionPlane.ts`, `World.ts`, `ThreeView.vue`, `App.vue`, `PaperService.ts`, and `ProjectService.ts` by line count (`frontend/src/components/workspace/SvgCanvas.vue:181`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:176`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:113`, `frontend/src/components/panels/ThreeView.vue:64`, `frontend/src/App.vue:106`, `frontend/src/services/PaperService.ts:108`, `frontend/src/services/ProjectService.ts:98`).
architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:11:The root package is a workspace wrapper over `frontend` and `backend`; root scripts delegate dev/build/test/lint to the frontend workspace and docs scripts to VitePress (`package.json:5`, `package.json:9`, `package.json:10`, `package.json:11`, `package.json:12`, `package.json:13`, `package.json:14`, `package.json:15`, `package.json:16`). The frontend package builds with `vue-tsc && vite build`, tests with Vitest, and runs Playwright e2e through `test:e2e` (`frontend/package.json:7`, `frontend/package.json:8`, `frontend/package.json:9`, `frontend/package.json:10`, `frontend/package.json:11`, `frontend/package.json:12`). The backend package has its own Express/TypeScript build and Vitest scripts but is not wired into root build/test scripts (`backend/package.json:7`, `backend/package.json:8`, `backend/package.json:9`, `backend/package.json:10`, `backend/package.json:11`).
architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:13:`frontend/src/main.ts` is the frontend entry point: it imports global styles, registers descriptors, creates the Vue app and Pinia, installs Pinia, and mounts to `#app` (`frontend/src/main.ts:24`, `frontend/src/main.ts:27`, `frontend/src/main.ts:28`, `frontend/src/main.ts:30`, `frontend/src/main.ts:32`). `frontend/src/App.vue` is the application shell. It imports UI panels/dialogs, the command stack, deletion factory, stores, `World`, Drive service, and `ProjectService` (`frontend/src/App.vue:106`, `frontend/src/App.vue:115`, `frontend/src/App.vue:117`, `frontend/src/App.vue:118`, `frontend/src/App.vue:123`, `frontend/src/App.vue:124`, `frontend/src/App.vue:125`). It owns a mutable `world` instance and a singleton `CommandStack` (`frontend/src/App.vue:147`, `frontend/src/App.vue:151`), provides the command stack to descendants (`frontend/src/App.vue:152`), initializes Drive/local project state (`frontend/src/App.vue:273`), and handles save/open/autosave/keyboard/delete/select-all behavior (`frontend/src/App.vue:375`, `frontend/src/App.vue:416`, `frontend/src/App.vue:472`, `frontend/src/App.vue:801`, `frontend/src/App.vue:838`, `frontend/src/App.vue:905`).
architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:15:The backend entry point is `backend/src/server.ts`, which creates the Express app and port, installs CORS and JSON middleware, mounts `/health` and `/api/projects`, and starts listening (`backend/src/server.ts:6`, `backend/src/server.ts:7`, `backend/src/server.ts:10`, `backend/src/server.ts:11`, `backend/src/server.ts:14`, `backend/src/server.ts:15`, `backend/src/server.ts:18`). Its project routes use a file-backed repository directly inside the router module (`backend/src/api/projects.ts:1`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:2`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:4`, `backend/src/api/projects.ts:5`).
architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:27:The current store layer is mixed. `toolStore` is a composable-style singleton rather than a Pinia `defineStore`; it reads and writes localStorage at module/use-site level to persist tool-family preferences (`frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts:50`, `frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts:51`, `frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts:53`, `frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts:61`, `frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts:64`, `frontend/src/stores/toolStore.ts:73`). `worldStore` is a Pinia store with separate `elements2D`, `elements3D`, `guides`, and `DependencyGraph` state (`frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:1`, `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:4`, `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:7`, `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:8`, `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:9`, `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:10`, `frontend/src/stores/worldStore.ts:13`). That duplicates the current domain ownership model in which `World` owns 3D objects and each `ProjectionPlane` owns 2D objects (`frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:14`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:15`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:115`, `frontend/src/domain/world/World.ts:119`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:190`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:191`, `frontend/src/domain/world/ProjectionPlane.ts:192`).
architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:29:Composables are UI/application helpers rather than domain model owners. For example, `useViewport` depends on `viewStore` (`frontend/src/composables/useViewport.ts:15`), while `useSnapping` and `useElementGeometry` read `worldStore` and `viewStore` rather than the canonical `World` object (`frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:2`, `frontend/src/composables/useSnapping.ts:3`, `frontend/src/composables/useElementGeometry.ts:11`, `frontend/src/composables/useElementGeometry.ts:12`). This creates a parallel UI-store pathway beside the newer `World`/projection-plane model.
architecture-audit/baseline/architecture-map.md:33:Interactive tools are mostly command builders. `ArgumentCollectorTool` imports selection masks, command, and tool context types, then collects arguments and pushes commands after validation (`frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:40`, `frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:41`, `frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:42`, `frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:43`, `frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:44`, `frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:66`, `frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:137`, `frontend/src/tools/ArgumentCollectorTool.ts:155`). Concrete tools directly import command operations, action creators, and process-tree operation helpers; e.g. `GuideTool` imports `Command`, guide sequence factory, process-tree action creators, process-tree operation classes, and action-group creation (`frontend/src/tools/GuideTool.ts:30`, `frontend/src/tools/GuideTool.ts:31`, `frontend/src/tools/GuideTool.ts:32`, `frontend/src/tools/GuideTool.ts:33`, `frontend/src/tools/GuideTool.ts:34`, `frontend/src/tools/GuideTool.ts:35`, `frontend/src/tools/GuideTool.ts:36`).
